{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Joshua:</b> Some say that the filthy garments refer to one of his grandsons, who became a son-in-law to Sanballat, and this sin is not upon Joshua, for this did not happen in his days. The correct view: that he did not have garments of glory and splendor, for they had only an altar to offer burnt offerings, and they had neither Temple nor curtain [parokhet] nor ark-cover [kaporet] nor golden altar nor golden garments. And so the garments are a metaphor that he has no glory or majesty."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:48.052141970Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}